{"uid":"b404e171064b817d","name":"test_steering_entry_appears_pending_then_flips_to_applied","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_steering_entry_appears_pending_then_flips_to_applied","historyId":"be6b90ec503426177d5c80025902024b","time":{"start":1791867517623,"stop":1791867534564,"duration":16941},"description":"Task 017 (#17) against a REAL engine: the panel's whole point is that a\n    queued message is visibly *pending* until the loop reads it at an\n    iteration boundary, and *applied* afterwards -- so an operator can tell\n    \"the agent has not seen this yet\" from \"the agent has it\".\n\n    Steered through the hub's own form (the write surface #17 says was the\n    only surface), then watched through the same page.\n\n    Task 070 (steer 005 defect 2): the run's FIRST worker iteration is held\n    open (`STUB_HOLD_FILE`/`STUB_HOLD_PHASE=\"worker\"`, the same bounded\n    barrier task 064 used for the liveness proof) from before the browser\n    even opens the page, and released only once `#steer-status` has shown\n    \"sent\" -- i.e. the POST /steering has already been accepted -- so the\n    engine can never answer 409 \"job finished / steering has no effect\"\n    because the loop raced ahead to a terminal state while Playwright was\n    still filling the form. Before this fix the hold did not exist: a\n    fast loop (STUB_SLEEP=\"1\" across 8 iterations, no barrier) could finish\n    the whole run inside the real wall-clock time Playwright needs to open\n    the page and submit, which is exactly the failure this bounded hold\n    rules out rather than papering over with a longer sleep or more\n    iterations.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 017 (#17) against a REAL engine: the panel's whole point is that a<br />\nqueued message is visibly <em>pending</em> until the loop reads it at an<br />\niteration boundary, and <em>applied</em> afterwards -- so an operator can tell<br />\n&quot;the agent has not seen this yet&quot; from &quot;the agent has it&quot;.</p>\n<pre><code>Steered through the hub's own form (the write surface #17 says was the\nonly surface), then watched through the same page.\n\nTask 070 (steer 005 defect 2): the run's FIRST worker iteration is held\nopen (`STUB_HOLD_FILE`/`STUB_HOLD_PHASE=&quot;worker&quot;`, the same bounded\nbarrier task 064 used for the liveness proof) from before the browser\neven opens the page, and released only once `#steer-status` has shown\n&quot;sent&quot; -- i.e. the POST /steering has already been accepted -- so the\nengine can never answer 409 &quot;job finished / steering has no effect&quot;\nbecause the loop raced ahead to a terminal state while Playwright was\nstill filling the form. Before this fix the hold did not exist: a\nfast loop (STUB_SLEEP=&quot;1&quot; across 8 iterations, no barrier) could finish\nthe whole run inside the real wall-clock time Playwright needs to open\nthe page and submit, which is exactly the failure this bounded hold\nrules out rather than papering over with a longer sleep or more\niterations.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866936748,"stop":1791866936748,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866936749,"stop":1791866936749,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791867517620,"stop":1791867517620,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"